title: Case Manager › Active cases › Open a case from the tracker
route: /manager → /authorizations/case/ID
intro: The case ID and the 'Open' button open the case page. A click on the row itself opens the quick view instead, and its 'Open case' button reaches the same page. A case that is a request gets the Authorizations case page; a case that only the ledger has gets the Ledger case page; a case at a site the viewer is not looking at gets the out-of-site card. None dead-ends.
dir: TD
also: Reviews work the same way: 'Open case' in the review drawer uses the same pages.
---
start s1 "Tracker row is on screen"
click c1 "Click anywhere on the row that is not a button\n(or its quick view button)"
goto gq "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Quick view of a case"
click c2 "Click the case ID (underlined)"
click c3 "Click 'Open' at the end of the row"
process p0 "A click on the ID or on a button acts on its own, and the row ignores it: the case opens once and Back needs one press"
process p1 "Case Manager works out the address\n/authorizations/case/ followed by the case code"
decision d1 "Is the row a denial?"
process p2 "Uses the case the denial came from\nD-3318 opens R-0997, the original case"
process p3 "Uses the row's own ID\nfor example R-1042, I-2207 or R-0856"
decision dsite "Is the case at a site the viewer is looking at?"
screen sos "Out-of-site card\n'This case is not available at Site A'\nNo patient or detail"
goto gs "Continues in: Case Manager › Sites › What each site sees and out-of-site links"
decision d2 "Is the case a request in the queue or on the Dashboard?\n(30 of the 56 rows, and every case signed and sent today)"
screen s2 "Case page\nHeader with the case ID, level of care and the request clock\nTabs for the case"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case"
decision d3 "Is the case in the Case Manager ledger?\n(the other 26 rows)"
screen s3 "Ledger case page\nSummary from the ledger record, next step and history\nButtons 'Open the review' (when one is due) and 'Back to Case Manager'"
goto g3 "Continues in: Case Manager › Ledger case › Open and read"
screen s5 "'Request not found'\n'There is no request with the ID R-9999.'\n(only for an address typed by hand)"
click c5 "Click the browser Back button"
screen s4 "Case Manager again\nSame tab, but search, filters, sort and page are back to their defaults"
process p5 "These live in the page, not in the address, so they are not remembered"
end e1 "Back at the top of the tracker"

s1 --> c1 & c2 & c3
c3 --> p0 --> p1
c1 --> gq
c2 --> p1
gq -.-> p1
p1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> dsite
d1 -->|No| p3 --> dsite
dsite -->|No| sos --> gs
dsite -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Yes| s2 --> g1
d2 -->|No| d3
d3 -->|Yes| s3 --> g3
d3 -.->|No| s5
s2 --> c5
s3 --> c5
c5 --> s4 --> p5 --> e1
